#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pr-triage — prioritize a GitHub PR's diff for human review using local Claude.

Takes a PR link, fetches the diff via `gh`, asks the locally-configured
`claude` CLI to score every hunk (0-100 importance, category, one-line
reason), and prints the diff re-ordered by review priority. Obvious noise
(lockfiles, generated code, binaries, pure renames, whitespace-only changes)
is pre-scored heuristically and never sent to the model.

Requires: gh (authenticated), claude CLI. Honors whatever backend your
shell configures for claude (Anthropic login, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL -> LM Studio,
Bedrock, ...). No third-party Python deps.

Examples:
  pr-triage https://github.com/Nextdoor/dataflow/pull/123
  pr-triage Nextdoor/dataflow#123 --top 10
  pr-triage 123 --repo Nextdoor/dataflow --model sonnet --html report.html
  pr-triage serve                           # start the triage server (dashboard + overlay)
  pr-triage Nextdoor/dataflow#123 --serve   # triage, then serve (or publish into running server)
  pr-triage logs -n 50 -f                   # tail the server log
  pr-triage purge Nextdoor/dataflow#123     # drop one stored triage (omit PR: purge all)
"""

